        "description": "Receives the webhook POST request fired by the **UACF7 (Ultra Addons for Contact Form 7)** plugin on your WordPress site whenever a visitor submits a Contact Form 7 form.\n\n### Trigger\nAutomatically called by UACF7 after a successful CF7 form submission. No manual invocation needed in production — use this request to test your webhook setup.\n\n### What happens after receiving\nThe post-response script:\n1. Parses the JSON body and stores `name`, `email`, `message`, and `submitted_at` as collection variables\n2. Fires a staff notification email via the Resend API\n3. Fires a confirmation email back to the form submitter\n\n### UACF7 Field Mapping\nIn your UACF7 webhook settings, map your CF7 fields to these JSON keys:\n\n| CF7 Field Tag | JSON Key |\n|---|---|\n| `[text* your-name]` | `name` |\n| `[email* your-email]` | `email` |\n| `[textarea your-message]` | `message` |\n\n### Mock Endpoint\nThe URL points to a Postman mock server for testing. Replace with your production endpoint URL when deploying."
      },
